Q: Golang - convert [8]bool to byte A: <p><strong>Golang - convert [8]bool to uint8</strong>
<em>(8 boolean flags to 8 bits)</em></p>
<p>This solution is probably faster, avoiding the bit shifting for every bit, more straighforward to understand, beginner friendly.</p>
<pre><code>    **transform  flags into actual bits:**
    [ true true false false]  -&gt; [ high high low low] -&gt; 1100 -&gt; 12
    [ true false false true]  -&gt; [ high low low high] -&gt; 1001 -&gt; 9 
</code></pre>
<p><strong>playground link, runnable code</strong>:</p>
<p><a href="https://goplay.tools/snippet/GXlOnaQW_u2" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://goplay.tools/snippet/GXlOnaQW_u2</a></p>
<pre class="lang-golang prettyprint-override"><code>

    // ConvertToByte - sums only a few predefined weights
    // Faster version (avoiding the bit shift, for every bit)
    // accepts only an array as asked by the OP,[8]bool

    func ConvertToByte (mei [8]bool) uint8 {
        bits := [8]uint8{0b10000000, 0b01000000, 0b00100000, 0b00010000, 0b00010000, 0b00000100, 0b00000010, 0b00000001}

        var result uint8

        for i, b := range mei {
            if b {
                result += bits[i] // operates only on the '1' bits
            }
        }
        return result
    }




</code></pre>

